  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The recurrence returns to the DQ-CTM thought stage, while encode and decode stay outside the loop.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes a dense carrier before any compact thought process runs. The carrier is split into windows, so the thought process can work locally. The repeated ticks return only to the DQ-CTM stage, not to the encoder or decoder. The tick box uses shared parameters across the recurrence. The decoder reads the updated dense carrier after the thought ticks finish.",
