    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first makes a dense feature field, then partitions that field into windows without changing its source.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field F. The dense field is the object carried forward into the rest of the method. The window operator partitions F into X. The equation keeps the carrier visible across the partition step.",
